{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nDuring a commercial-driver review after a refrigerated-freight run, the nurse brings together the driver's account, a dated clinical attachment and an employer form copied from an earlier assessment; the documents refer to different times, and the current entry distinguishes a completed examination from recollections, plans and information concerning another person.\n\nThe current ophthalmologist confirms monocular vision following a remote injury and measures visual acuity of 6/9 in the remaining eye, with a horizontal field of 145 degrees measured within 10 degrees above and below the horizontal midline; the signed specialist report explicitly finds no other significant field loss likely to impede driving, whereas an old binocular screening entry describes the driver's condition before the injury and is retained only as historical context.\n\nThe driver alternates urban deliveries with a longer motorway leg and describes a busy depot where engine noise, glare and interrupted meals can complicate an account of symptoms; the nurse records the work setting as context, while keeping the dated clinical findings distinct from the driver's explanation for why a symptom might have occurred on that shift.\n\nThe record is prepared for the reviewing clinician with the sequence of events and the provenance of the available findings intact, because the employer summary and the driver's account answer different questions; a completed test is retained as such, but an unresolved detail is not filled in from a family member's history or from an earlier document with different testing conditions.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
